---
/**
 * /privacy/
 *
 * PDPA privacy policy. The section that matters most for a matching service is
 * disclosure: the details go to the team behind Junk to Clear, which passes
 * them to the partner firm that will quote. The form's notice says the same.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { company } from '../lib/data';
import { urls } from '../lib/urls';
import { meta } from '../lib/seo';

const path = urls.privacy();
const { title, description } = meta(
  'Privacy Policy | AirconToCool',
  'How AirconToCool collects, uses and discloses personal data under Singapore’s PDPA, including passing enquiries to partner aircon firms.',
);

const lastUpdated = '5 October 2026';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path={path} crumbs={[{ name: 'Privacy policy', path }]}>
  <section class="border-b border-line bg-surface">
    <div class="wrap-narrow py-12 sm:py-16">
      <img src="/illo/privacy.svg" alt="An enquiry form behind a shield with a padlock" width="480" height="300" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" class="mb-6 h-auto w-full max-w-xs" />
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold sm:text-4xl">Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-ink-muted">
        How {company.tradingName} handles your personal data under Singapore’s Personal Data
        Protection Act 2012 (PDPA).
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-faint">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap-narrow prose-ac py-12 text-ink-muted sm:py-16">
    <div class="rounded-card border border-brand/25 bg-brand-light/50 p-5 text-ink">
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="font-semibold">The short version.</strong> {company.tradingName} is a
        matching service, not an aircon company. When you send an enquiry, your details
        go to the team behind {company.parentBrand}, which passes them to the partner
        aircon firm that will quote you. That is the point of the service, and the form
        says so before you send it. We don’t sell your data.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      This site is run by the team behind {company.parentBrand}, operated by
      <strong>{company.entityName}</strong>. In this policy, “we”, “us” and “our” mean that
      team. {company.tradingName} introduces homes and businesses in Singapore to independent
      aircon firms. We don’t service or repair aircons ourselves.
    </p>

    <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
    <p>Through the enquiry form, we collect:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
      <li>your name and phone or WhatsApp number;</li>
      <li>the service, the number and type of units, your property type, your area and when you need the work done;</li>
      <li>anything else you write in the form;</li>
      <li>the page you sent the enquiry from.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We also collect non-identifying usage data through Google Analytics, such as which
      pages were viewed and whether an enquiry was sent. This site doesn’t use browser local
      storage or session storage.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Why we collect it</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
      <li>To understand and respond to your enquiry.</li>
      <li>To pass your enquiry to a partner aircon firm that can quote you.</li>
      <li>To follow up on your enquiry, and on any problem with a job we passed on.</li>
      <li>To keep records of enquiries and improve this site.</li>
      <li>To meet legal or regulatory obligations.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Who we pass it to</h2>
    <p>
      When you send an enquiry, we pass your name, phone number and the details of the job
      to the partner aircon firm that will quote you, so it can contact you directly.
      Occasionally we may pass it to a second firm, for example if the first can’t take the
      job. We don’t sell personal data, and we don’t pass it to advertisers or unrelated
      businesses.
    </p>
    <p>
      Once a firm has your details, it is a separate organisation with its own obligations
      under the PDPA. Any agreement for the aircon work is between you and that firm.
    </p>
    <p>
      We also use service providers to run this site and deliver enquiries, including a
      form-delivery service, hosting and Google Analytics, and we disclose data where the
      law requires it.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Consent, and withdrawing it</h2>
    <p>
      The form tells you where your details will go before you send it. By sending it, you
      consent to that use. You can withdraw consent at any time by contacting us (section 9).
      We’ll stop using your data for these purposes within a reasonable time. We can’t
      recall details already passed to a firm, so you would need to contact that firm too.
    </p>

    <h2>6. How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      We keep enquiry data for as long as we need it for the purposes above, and then for up
      to <strong>24 months</strong> from your last contact with us, so we can deal with
      follow-up questions about a job. After that we delete or anonymise it, unless the law
      requires us to keep it longer.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Access and correction</h2>
    <p>
      Under the PDPA you can ask us for access to the personal data we hold about you, and
      how it has been used or disclosed in the past year, and ask us to correct anything
      inaccurate. We may need to verify your identity first, and a reasonable fee may apply
      to an access request, as the PDPA allows.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Protecting your data</h2>
    <p>
      We make reasonable security arrangements to protect the personal data we hold against
      unauthorised access, use, disclosure or loss. No transmission over the internet is
      completely secure.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Send questions, access or correction requests and consent withdrawals through the
      <a href={urls.contact()}>contact form</a>, marked for the attention of the Data
      Protection Officer.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy. The date at the top shows when it last changed.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Complaints</h2>
    <p>
      If you’re not satisfied with how we’ve handled your data, contact us first. You can
      also complain to the Personal Data Protection Commission of Singapore.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
